1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Kerstin Albrechtsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Albrecht Hansson (Svinhufvud) and Bengta Nilsdotter Hästhuvud
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Knut Knutsson,''' Bergsman, Varggården, St Kopparberg Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Knutsson, g. married a daughter of judge Albrecht Hansson Swinhufwud in Aspe-was an assistant in the Mining Court and a churchwarden like the brothers Jacob and Pehr. the one gang in his cabin on Gammelberget, they began to a
2 CONC rgue about the cabin, then he took the cabin bellows on his shoulder and carried it home and let them fight. He was killed by two brothers in a cellar in Falun®), they must give his murderers "these plates were as visible as large
2 CONC  bricks". He had a servant Carl Erichsson, who when he drove after the dead man took the keys out of his knapsack and went home and took a large pile of money from his chest; He then became a great miner [fourth party winner in 16
2 CONC 40], who worked in Damshyttan and was called Svad-den in Roteboo, because he bought this homestead from King Gustaf Adolf (southeast of Käll-slätten, then belonging to Bokhäll. Swab's heirs). "But how did it end with He deceived s
2 CONC ome gentlemen in the Mining League, that there was an ore streak in his cellar, it was a lie, he had to cut off the street for the mistake. He finally became so angry that at Constans Colwin's Cellar he soaked up the same homestea
2 CONC d in beer and wine, then walked with a basket on his arm and made sausage sticks for the wine people and finally died in a cabin. His son-in-law Hans Carlsson Plogbilen gave his father-in-law an earful and had to cut his throat fo
2 CONC r it. All according to Jacob Ingelsson - moving images of the times.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000218829711822&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://archive.org/details/MedDallvenFrrnKLlornaTillHavetDelIIIBok4/page/n167/mode/2up?q=Knut  '''Med Dalälven Från Källorna Till Havet Del III Bok 4 Stora Kopparberg, by Karl Erik Forsslund''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In the same year, the following were taxed in Varregärden: K. M.'s farmer Hinriick Nilsson, Mortthin Mickilsson, Hans Jönsson and H:u Kirstin. And in 1612: Jöran Ersson (see above 159S), Jonas in Wargärden, Carl ibid., Knut Knutss
2 CONC on (sölfskiedh, father) Knutsson (sölfskiedar 2, last Pedersson's sons — he had 7, the others were Hans in Lunsta, Pähr in Wargärden Anders in Hedmora (father of councilman Johan Andersson there, + 1697) - and 3 daughters. of whom
2 CONC  Malin (+ 1595) became the husband of Christopher Olsson in Noor and Margareta with the churchwarden Michael Michaelis in Svärdsjoe) can thus also count the farm among their ancestors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Knutsson, the husband of a daughter of the judge Albrecht Hansson Swinhufwud in Aspevar, assistant in the Mining Court and churchwarden, like the brothers Pehr, the latter a strong man: he was once in his cabin on Gammelberge
2 CONC t, they began to quarrel about the cabin, then he took the cabin bell on his shoulder and carried it home and let them quarrel. He was killed by two brothers in a cellar in Falun®), they had to give his murderer 8 shippund of Plat
2 CONC e-Copper, "these plates were as big as bricks". He had a servant Carl Erichsson, who when he drove after the dead man took the keys out of his village locker and went home and took a large pile of money from his chest; He then bec
2 CONC ame a great miner [fourth party winner in 1640], who worked in Damshyttan and was called Svad-den 1 Roteboo, because he bought this homestead from King Gustaf Adolf (southeast of Küll-slätten, then belonging to Bokhäll. Swab's hei
2 CONC rs). >But what happened to this Swadden in Roteboo?» He fooled some gentlemen in the Mining College, that there was an ore streak in his cellar, it was a lie, he had to quit street running for the job. He finally became so angry t
2 CONC hat at Constans Colwin's cellar he soaked the same homestead in beer and wine, then walked with a basket on his arm and made sausage sticks that the gwin people eventually died out of it. His son-in-law Hans Carlsson Plogbilen gav
2 CONC e his father-in-law a slap in the face and therefore had to cut his throat. All according to Jacob Ingelsson - leran-de time pictures.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT *  With the Dalälven River From the Sources to the Sea Part III Book 4 Stora Kopparberg - https://archive.org/details/MedDallvenFrrnKLlornaTillHavetDelIIIBok4/page/n127/mode/2up?q=Knut
