1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svinhufvud_af_Qvalstad_nr_145 '''Hans Persson, till Surarve''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Erhöll konung Gustaf I:s brev i 1534, "Ändock hans svärfader Måns Nilsson på Asbo förbrutit allt vad han ägde, förunnades denne hans måg en gård Surarve med all den del därtill lyder". 
2 CONT * Very interesting in that collection of copies, some news (at least for me) for example the following is mentioned on 10 Feb 1578 "Come for the right wife Anna in Noret the late Hans Persson's wife in Asboda, mädh sine children, 
2 CONC and addressed Nils Hansson at Sundeborgen , that he would have them the same home Suneborgen from which her husband's father and the children's father Per Siurdsson in Fremundeby had bought for 14 Shippounds of copper money, 100 m
2 CONC arks of money and 10 cubits of learning and a sölff spoon, and beuiste dedh with a parchment purchase letter with hanging the signet, which they presented in court as dated was anno A 1518..." this therefore refers to the parents 
2 CONC and grandfather of the noble Per Hansson (Svinhufvud af Qvalstad) whose mother apparently remarried and settled in Noret! (Kopiesamlingen I (f d Manuscript collection), Department 1, Manuscript collections in alphabetical order (R
2 CONC A) 148 (0-9999) Image 850 (AID: v913991.b850).
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000006127713586?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000194353339854 Very interesting in that collection of copies, some news (at least for me) for example the following is mentioned on 10 Fe
2 CONC b 1578 "Come for the right wife Anna in Noret the late Hans Persson's wife in Asboda, mädh sine children, and addressed Nils Hansson at Sundeborgen , that he would have them the same home Suneborgen from which her husband's father
2 CONC  and the children's father Per Siurdsson in Fremundeby had bought for 14 Shippounds of copper money, 100 marks of money and 10 cubits of learning and a sölff spoon, and beuiste dedh with a parchment purchase letter with hanging th
2 CONC e signet, which they presented in court as dated was anno A 1518..." this therefore refers to the parents and grandfather of the noble Per Hansson (Svinhufvud af Qvalstad) whose mother apparently remarried and settled in Noret! (K
2 CONC opiesamlingen I (f d Manuscript collection), Department 1, Manuscript collections in alphabetical order (RA) 148 (0-9999) Image 850 (AID: v913991.b850)).]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Noble Family Svinhufvud af Qvalstad No. 145=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Knighted 1574-06-22, Introd. 1625. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The families Svinhufvud af Qvalstad and Svinhufvud in Västergötland descended both from the female line of an old noble family in Dalarna, which was named Svinhufvud after its heraldic image and whose weapons both families took up
2 CONC  at the knighting . As far as we know, they do not share more common origin than that the knighted ancestor of the dynasty Svinhufvud in Västergötland, Daniel Torkilsson, was married to a cousin of the knighted progenitor of the d
2 CONC ynasty Svinhufvud af Qvalstad Peder Hansson or granddaughter of the latter's grandfather, Peder Jönsson Skrifvare. The well-known Bishop of Vasteras Otto, who died in 1522, belonged to the famous noble family in the Dales, which c
2 CONC arried a six-pointed star in the weapon, but he adopted his maturnal namn and weapons, and used a squared shield with a star and the Svinhufvud coat of arms. The dynasty Svinhufvud af Qvalstad is thought to have come to Sweden fro
2 CONC m Norway, where it is supposed to have been nobility. It was introduced as Nobility in Finland in 1818 under No. 7 among nobles and has not been represented in Sweden efter Finland's annexation to Russia in 1809.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 WA. 2 Al. 3 Letter in Sjöholms archive [AT (Sch)]. 4 AT (Sch), 5 SH, liber caus, Vol. 54 (OA). 6 Ridd. o. Ad. protocol. 7 WA. 8 f. 9 f. 10 Epitafiet Värmdö church (UFF). 11 Um. 12 Sv. 13 KA köpegodsakt 263 (OA). 14 Large Church 
2 CONC marriage records. 15 Härads Assembly Christening 1739. 16 Härads Assembly dödbok 1775. 17 OA, part 5, p. 239. 18 At (P). 19 Vallentuna judgment book. 20 Febr. 1922 (OA). 21 Ka, reduktionskommissionena process documents, Upland IV,
2 CONC  born 710 (OA). 22 Långhundra härads judgment book (OA.). 23 SH, liber caus. Vol. 122, pars 7 (OA). 24 Sh, liber caus, Vol. 135, pars 8 (OA). 25 Bälingesjön härads judgment book (OA). 26 Messaging. of West Heather Fors, Malmo. 27 
2 CONC GIR. 28 SH liber caus, Vol. 132 (OA). 29 Bridge härads judgment book 1677 (OA). 30 Seven hundred härads judgment book 1696 (OA). 31 1: Best provincial office expedition 1723, kammarkollegii archive (OA). 32 Selebo härads deed prot
2 CONC ein. 12 June 1745 (OA). 33 Långhundra härads judgment book 25 June 1724 (OA). 34 Messaging. P. Married Vejde, Vaxjo. 35 SRB. 36 Uff.
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************************************** Living at Surarve, Aspeboda, Dalarna
2 CONT
2 CONT Bergsman. Fick av Gustav Vasa ägorätt i Måns Nilssons indragna gods
2 CONT
2 CONT Den 9 sep 1534 fick Hans Persson Gustav Vasas förläningsbrev på gården Surarvet i Aspeboda och den 2 sep 1536 på ytterligare sex av Måns Nilssons tidigare gårdar. 1539 brukade H själv fortfarande Surarvet, Harmstäkt, och en gård i
2 CONC  Sundborn samt drev kopparbruk i stor skala. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tillsammans med sin bror domaren Jöns Persson på Risholm viid Hosjön ägde han även en av två gårdar i Främby (den andra tillhörde Jöns måg Daniel Torkelsson). 
2 CONT
2 CONT År 1551 bytte Gustav Vasa till sig gården i Främby för att använda den som fogdesäte. Som ersättning fick Hans dels den definitiva äganderätten till Stora Aspeboda (som han tycks ha övertagit efter svärmodern 1548) dels gårdarna V
2 CONC ilkesbacke, Barkarbacken och Vikerbacken. Främby tycks dock ha återgått till Hans ättlingar så småningom.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svinhufvud_af_Qvalstad_nr_145#TAB_4
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Persson , to Surarve in Aspeboda parish, Kopparberg, be him 1534-02-20 (9/9) received King Gustavus I's letter, that 'nevertheless his father in law Måns Nilsson Asbo forfeit all that he had, vouchsafed him his måg a farm Sur
2 CONC arve with all the part thereto reads'. Was still alive in 1568 and brought into force the Red Pig Head in golden fields. 27 . Married to Anna Månsdotter , daughter of the steward of Copper Mountain Måns Nilsson Asbo (Aspeboda), th
2 CONC e rebellious conspiracies beheaded and steglad 1532, which was a Danish nobleman's family, which the Force brought a red pig head in golden fields, and Margareta Albrektsdotter Björnram.
