1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anna Månsdotter (Svinhufvud)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Måns Nilsson Svinhufvud and Margreta Albrechtsdotter Björnram
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svinhufvud_af_Qvalstad_nr_145 Noble family Svinhufvud of Qvalstad no. 145]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peder Jönsson Scrivener , to Främmandeby (Främby) in Falu county,''' assembly, in which he inherited part with his wife. Bailiff in Dalarne 1476. Became district governor in Dalarne in 1480 on behalf of Nils Sture. Ord. judge
2 CONC  there. 1484–1501. Still alive in 1516 and then living in Risholn. '''Married to Barbro Johansdotter , who carried two stag horns in a blue field in the coat of arms, daughter of Johan Hjort and Brita Jönsdotter of the old Svinhuf
2 CONC vudssläkten.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Hans Persson ,''' to Surarve in Aspeboda parish, Kopparberg county, where on 1534-02-20 (9/9) he received a letter from King Gustaf I, stating that 'although his father-in-law Måns Nilsson at Asbo had destroyed everything he 
2 CONC owned, he was granted to his son-in-law a farm Surarve with all the parts that belong to it'. Still alive in 1568 and carried in his coat of arms a red Pig's Head in a golden field. 27. '''Married to Anna Månsdotter , daughter of 
2 CONC the bailiff at Kopparberget Måns Nilsson at Asbo (Aspeboda), beheaded and scalded for rebellious stampings in 1532, who was of a Danish free family, which carried in its coat of arms a red Pig's Head in a golden field, and Margare
2 CONC ta Albrektsdotter Björnram.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Per Hansson ,''' ennobled Svinhufvud, to Främby and Surarve. Was mining bailiff at Salberget in 1569. Received on 28/2 in fief three homesteads in the parishes of Torsång and Kopparberg, which had in fact gone to King Gustaf 
2 CONC I after his maternal grandfather, and then registered at Holm in Tuna parish, Kopparberg county. Bailiff in Eastern and Western Dalarna 1570–1574 and in Western Silvberg county 1574 2 . Received maintenance letter 2 1572-08-19. En
2 CONC nobled 1574-06-22. Was district governor in Jönåker district, Södermanland county 1577 3 and then registered at Almby 3 in Jäder parish, Södermanland county (father-in-law's property). Died before 1579 2 . His coat of arms was ere
2 CONC cted in Vansö church 4 Södermanland county. Married to Agneta Körning , to Märinge in Strängnäs' county assembly (on Tosterön) in her 2nd marriage (married 1st 1557-06-15 [morning gift] at Almby to the squire and commander over Ko
2 CONC rsholm and Ostrobothnia Nils Ottosson, of the old horse-head family, to Holm and Årby, in his 2nd marriage [married 1st 1542-02-20, when he gave Holm as a morning gift, to Anna Persdotter, daughter of Per Larsson (Ulfstand), to År
2 CONC by and Hallkved, and hh Elin]). She was still alive in 1608, daughter of the knight chief Matts Körning and Beata Kuse.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Carl Persson''' . Assessor. Died 1634. See Tab. 2.
2 CONT * '''Jöns Persson .''' Bailiff. Died 1636. See Tab. 4.
2 CONT * '''Lars Persson .''' Was present at the inheritance change at Ekenäs 1604-04-12 after his aunt Mrs. Ingela Körning.[ 5 ]
2 CONT * '''Erik Persson .''' Was present at the aforementioned inheritance. [ 5 ]
2 CONT * '''Justina Persdotter,''' from Rosendal in Strängnäs' county assembly, lived in 1647. Married to Johan Eriksson, from Rosendal , who lived in 1613.
