1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Per Hansson Svinhufvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Hans Persson, till Surarve (Svinhufvud) and Anna Månsdotter 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/34993 His older brother Per Hansson (d sometime between 1577–79) was judge over Bergslagen and Dalarna in 1566–67, bailiff in various fiefdoms in Bergslagen 1569–74 and district chie
2 CONC f in Jönåker's district in Södermanland in 1577. He is said to have been ennobled in 1574 and wrote first to his wife Agneta's seat farm Holm in Stora Tuna parish, later to her farm Almby in Jäders parish, Södermanland. She was th
2 CONC e daughter of the county sheriff in Åker, Södermanland, Mats Körning (vol. 22, p. 16) and the granddaughter of the castle bailiff Erik Kuse (vol. 21) , who was executed at the Stockholm massacre .]
2 CONT * From about 1569 the family lived on the wife's ancestral farm Almby in Jäder sn in Södermanland
2 CONT * In 1574, the eldest son Per received a royal letter of shield and became the ancestor of the noble family Svinhufvud af Qvalstad. One of the descendants became president of Finland in 1931
2 CONT * Knighted in 1574 and adopted the boar's head as a coat of arms after his grandfather but with the colors black on a blue background. His family was later named Svinhufvud by Qualstad
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000008021420765&photo_id=6000000194349881844&position=0 In Dalarna's documents in 1610, a royal letter dated Gripsholm 23 Feb 1579 mentions "ärligh og welbördigh ku
2 CONC inne, wife Agneta till Holm, framledne Peder Hansson's effterleffuerska". The man was therefore dead on this date (Landskapshandling, Lan… hoar seejn.]
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000008021420765?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000194353370822 Regarding Per Hansson, here is an image from the fief register over Västmanland 1569-1573 (Strödda rekänskaper og handling
2 CONC en til 1630, Strödda rekänskaper og handlingen til 1630 Förläningsregister, SE/RA/5101/5101.18/5 (1560-1631), image id: A0070968_00215).]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svinhufvud_af_Qvalstad_nr_145 '''Per Hansson''', ''adlad'' '''Svinhufvud, till Främby och Surarve'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Per Hansson,''' ennobled Svinhufvud, to Främby and Surarve. Was a mining bailiff at Salberget in 1569. On 28/2, he received a fief of three homesteads in the parishes of Torsång and Kopparberg, which fell to King Gustaf I in th
2 CONC e case of his maternal grandfather, and then wrote to Holm in Tuna parish, Kopparberg county. Bailiff in Öster- and Väster-Dalarne 1570–1574 and in Västra Silvberg county 1574 2 . Received maintenance letter 2 1572-08-19. Knighted
2 CONC  22-06-1574. He was district chief in Jönåker's district Södermanland county in 1577 3 and then registered to Almby 3 in Jäders parish, Södermanland county (father-in-law's property). Death before 1579 2 . His coat of arms was set
2 CONC  up in Vansö church 4 Södermanland county. '''Married to Agneta Körning, to Märinge in Strängnäs' county council.''' (on Tosterön) in her '''2nd marriage (married 1st 1557-06-15 [morning gift] at Almby to the squire and commander 
2 CONC over Korsholm and Ostrobothnia Nils Ottosson, of the old horse head family, to Holm and Årby, in his 2nd married [married 1st 1542-02-20, when he gave Holm as a present, to Anna Persdotter, daughter of Per Larsson (Ulfstand), to Å
2 CONC rby and Hallkved, and hh Elin.'''] She was still alive in 1608, the daughter of the Jack chieftain Matts Körning and Beata Kuse.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Carl Persson,''' (son of Per Hansson, ennobled Svinhufvud, Tab. 1), to Märinge in Strängnäs' county council. and Torlaks in Nykyrko parish, Finland. Court junker. Belonged to King Sigismund's followers and therefore had to le
2 CONC ave the country in 1599 27 . Bailiff in Vemo district in Finland 1613–1614-11-00 2 . Service, assessor in Turku Court of Appeal 1627–1630. Witnessed the Riksdag in 1633 6 . Received authorization for the latter position in 1634 be
2 CONC fore 10/4, but died s. å. in Aug. 7 . His coat of arms was set up in Kimito church. Married in 1602 8 to Brita Agricola , lived in 1647 at Torlaks, but died in 1653 8 , daughter of the bishop of Reval Christian Agricola, ennobled 
2 CONC 1584-05-12, and Elin Fleming. Assessor. Died 1634.
2 CONT * '''Jöns Persson,''' Jöns Persson (son of Per Hansson, ennobled Svinhufvud, Tab. 1), to Kvalsta in Östuna parish, Stockholm county. Bailiff in Lång-och Sjuhundra hrad 1612, at Uppsala castle 1613 (fullm, 13/6)–1616, in Södertörn 
2 CONC 1616–1618 and again in Lång-och Sjuhundra hrad 1618–1620. Imprisoned in 1620 and requested in 1622 that his case be settled. Introduction 1627 under number 117, which was then changed to 145, and the family has since been named Sv
2 CONC inhufvud af Qvalstad. Died 15/10/1636 and buried on 18/12 in Östuna church, where his coat of arms was displayed and his tombstone was placed. Married to Margareta Månesköld af Seglinge , died 1650-04-03 at Kvalsta and buried 1651
2 CONC -01-06 in Östuna church, daughter of Christer Carlsson Månesköld (of Seglinge, no. 62) and his 1st wife Brita Björnsdotter ( Bååt ). Bailiff. Died 1636.
2 CONT * '''Lars Persson,'''  Was present at the transfer of inheritance at Ekenäs on 1604-04-12 after his aunt Mrs. Ingela Körning.[ 5 ]
2 CONT * '''Erik Persson,''' Be present at said inheritance. [ 5 ]
2 CONT * '''Justina Persdotter,''' to Rosendal in Strängnäs' county council, lived in 1647. Married to Johan Eriksson, to Rosendal , who lived in 1613.
