1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Knut Knutsson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Knut Pedersson i Varggården
2 CONT * Bergsman, Varggården, in Falun, Kopparberg, Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Kerstin Albrechtsdotter (Svinhufvud),''' Daughter of Albrecht Hansson (Svinhufvud) and Bengta Nilsdotter Hästhuvud and the granddaughter of Hans Persson, till Surarve and Anna Månsdotter (Svinhufvud).
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Knutsson, g. married a daughter of judge Albrecht Hansson Swinhufwud in Aspe-was an assistant in the Mining Court and a churchwarden like the brothers Jacob and Pehr. the one gang in his cabin on Gammelberget, they began to a
2 CONC rgue about the cabin, then he took the cabin bellows on his shoulder and carried it home and let them fight. He was killed by two brothers in a cellar in Falun®), they must give his murderers "these plates were as visible as large
2 CONC  bricks". He had a servant Carl Erichsson, who when he drove after the dead man took the keys out of his knapsack and went home and took a large pile of money from his chest; He then became a great miner [fourth party winner in 16
2 CONC 40], who worked in Damshyttan and was called Svad-den in Roteboo, because he bought this homestead from King Gustaf Adolf (southeast of Käll-slätten, then belonging to Bokhäll. Swab's heirs). "But how did it end with He deceived s
2 CONC ome gentlemen in the Mining League, that there was an ore streak in his cellar, it was a lie, he had to cut off the street for the mistake. He finally became so angry that at Constans Colwin's Cellar he soaked up the same homestea
2 CONC d in beer and wine, then walked with a basket on his arm and made sausage sticks for the wine people and finally died in a cabin. His son-in-law Hans Carlsson Plogbilen gave his father-in-law an earful and had to cut his throat fo
2 CONC r it. All according to Jacob Ingelsson - moving images of the times.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000218829711822&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://archive.org/details/MedDallvenFrrnKLlornaTillHavetDelIIIBok4/page/n167/mode/2up?q=Knut  '''Med Dalälven Från Källorna Till Havet Del III Bok 4 Stora Kopparberg, by Karl Erik Forsslund''']
2 CONT
2 CONT mention the homeowners Fr. Nordqvist and Erik Nordgvist (b. 1871, † 1932), as well as Falu city and Falu vicarage land in Varggärden. In a few older documents the different Varggärden have different designations. Werming's map of 
2 CONC 1810 has Warggärden close to the city border, Öf. Warggärden above it, Tab. Geogr. Store Wargegärden T mountain rescue guards south Lille Wargegärden's 3 owner shemman. Litzle Wargärden belonged to the properties registered after 
2 CONC Mäns Nilsson in Aspeboda, Pâl was a farmer there in 1539 Per Pâuelsson 1 Vindersmor was probably his son, K. M:ts land-IMAGE 192. FROM ÖVRA VARGGÄRDEN. FALU MINE AND farmer, who in 1571 was assessed for 5 skölp. copper and 2 goats
2 CONC , but no cow: Vindelsmora or Vimsäas the farm was later called, was perhaps one of the Nedra Varggardarna or in any event was nearby. According to C. J. Lundström, Nedre Varggärden, Löfberg and bergsfrälseegegendom in 1686, Varggä
2 CONC rden was another, Oluf Svensson and the ochlerian had arable land there in 1642. Otherwise, as a rule, only Varggärden or similar stands without further specification - so on the 1718 map Varggärden, on Nova Del. Wargärdsbygden. I
2 CONC t would therefore be difficult or impossible to determine in which of the farms the miner or the family lived. Mans Jönsson on Wargärden'). son of the mountaineer Jöns Hansson Swinhufwud on Höjen*) thus the div here is a member of
2 CONC  the Swinhufwudätten! But further back another family is found: Biörn in Wargärden believes Jacob Ingelsson was the first to settle there "250 years ago", that is, in the 1460s. Olof Biörnsson in Wargegärden received in 14813) fro
2 CONC m 10 Tuna residents confirmation of the right to use "all his captured forest" for his cabins at Spjutön (see above page 54): his son Jöns Olsson had the sons Hans, † approx. 1505, and Oluff Joensson (ionson, Jönsson) in Varghiega
2 CONC arden, who in 1505 executed a deed of sale*) and later mortgaged a fence in Longsio in Tuna to Stig Hansson, but his son-in-law Peder Andersson®) redeemed it again in 1560, and it was awarded in 1562 to one of his sons Pedersson (
2 CONC the other son Erik Persson was probably the father of Jöran Eriksson in Varggärden, who participated in the riot at Korgsarvet in 1598). The above Peer Andersson in Wargegärden was (according to Helmer Lagergren) daughter Anna, in
2 CONC ka 1539 and probably sister of bailiff Anders Olsson in Varggärden, both fourth party heirs as well as Jöns Olsson in Wargaalen, mentioned also in 1528 and 1542 Jöng Olsson in Wargegärden and his heirs Gustaf I's Open letter on 2/
2 CONC 3 in concerned Karin, He was probably*) son of mountaineer Olof Persson in Gammelberget and g. m. sister of Christopher Olsson's wife Anna in Rottneby and father of Mr. Nils in Huseby (Nicolaus, churchwarden 1 Husby 1541), whose s
2 CONC on Peder Nilsson owned Nygärden in Vika and Klingsbo in St. Skedvi. Either the aforementioned Knut Pedersson was the grandson or the grandson's granddaughter of Olof Biörnsson, then he was a great man, whose seal adorns a document
2 CONC  from 1556) (commander of this entire county in the time of King Eric and King John), has mostly lived on Kongsgärden with Borwin's Hyttegärd [in Falun] and had Wargärden as a homestead, writes Jacob Ingelsson: he is said to have 
2 CONC had a large homestead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blörn who followed him wherever he went, and ran for him when he came to Byss; a large granary stood still after him, larger than any here in the place. He had his Bench Room in the old Kiörckian. where now the Landzhöfding's benc
2 CONC h is, and his grave there with the tombstone K. E. F. 1925 PICTURE 193. STABLE AND STOVE AT ÖVRA VARGGÄRDEN. and his tomb on the old Predikstoln, which was removed in 1618. He died in 1580, was supposed to hurry away a rain shower
2 CONC , but was a big and strong man, then he fell over and died, before he came out. Sweden's richest miner in 1571, had gold, silver and other metals, 1500 marks in money and all kinds of cattle except pigs, all valued at 3688% marks.
2 CONC  In the same year, in Varregärden, K. M.'s farmer Hinriick Nilsson, Mortthin Mickilsson, Hans Jönsson and H:u Kirstin were taxed. And in 1612: Jöran Ersson (see above 159S), Jonas in Wargärden, Carl ibid., Knud Knutsson (sölfskied
2 CONC h, father) Knutsson (sölfskiedar 2, last Pedersson's sons,  he had 7, the others were Hans in Lunsta, Pähr in Wargärden Anders in Hedmora (father of councilman Johan Andersson there, + 1697) - and 3 daughters. of whom Malin (+ 159
2 CONC 5) became the wife of Christopher Olsson in Noor and Margareta with the parish priest Michael Michaelis in Svärdsjoe) can thus also count the farm among their ancestors. Knud Knutsson, wife of a daughter of the judge Albrecht Hans
2 CONC son Swinhufwud in Aspevar, assistant in the Mining Court and churchwarden, like the brothers Pehr, the latter a strong man: he was once in his cabin on Gammelberget, they began to quarrel about the cabin, then he took the cabin be
2 CONC ll on his shoulder and carried it home and let them quarrel. He was killed by two brothers in a cellar in Falun®), they had to give his killer 8 shippunds of Plate-Copper, "these plates were so visible as large bricks". He had a s
2 CONC ervant Carl Erichsson, who when he drove after the dead man took the keys out of his village lock and went
2 CONT
2 CONT In the same year, the following were taxed in Varregärden: K. M.'s farmer Hinriick Nilsson, Mortthin Mickilsson, Hans Jönsson and H:u Kirstin. And in 1612: Jöran Ersson (see above 159S), Jonas in Wargärden, Carl ibid., Knut Knutss
2 CONC on (sölfskiedh, father) Knutsson (sölfskiedar 2, last Pedersson's sons — he had 7, the others were Hans in Lunsta, Pähr in Wargärden Anders in Hedmora (father of councilman Johan Andersson there, + 1697) - and 3 daughters. of whom
2 CONC  Malin (+ 1595) became the husband of Christopher Olsson in Noor and Margareta with the churchwarden Michael Michaelis in Svärdsjoe) can thus also count the farm among their ancestors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Knut Knutsson, the husband of a daughter of the judge Albrecht Hansson Swinhufwud in Aspevar, assistant in the Mining Court and churchwarden,''' like the brothers Pehr, the latter a strong man: he was once in his cabin on Gamme
2 CONC lberget, they began to quarrel about the cabin, then he took the cabin bell on his shoulder and carried it home and let them quarrel. He was killed by two brothers in a cellar in Falun®), they had to give his murderer 8 shippund o
2 CONC f Plate-Copper, "these plates were as big as bricks". He had a servant Carl Erichsson, who when he drove after the dead man took the keys out of his village locker and went home and took a large pile of money from his chest; He th
2 CONC en became a great miner [fourth party winner in 1640], who worked in Damshyttan and was called Svad-den 1 Roteboo, because he bought this homestead from King Gustaf Adolf (southeast of Küll-slätten, then belonging to Bokhäll. Swab
2 CONC 's heirs). >But what happened to this Swadden in Roteboo?» He fooled some gentlemen in the Mining College, that there was an ore streak in his cellar, it was a lie, he had to quit street running for the job. He finally became so a
2 CONC ngry that at Constans Colwin's cellar he soaked the same homestead in beer and wine, then walked with a basket on his arm and made sausage sticks that the gwin people eventually died out of it. His son-in-law Hans Carlsson Plogbil
2 CONC en gave his father-in-law a slap in the face and therefore had to cut his throat. All according to Jacob Ingelsson - leran-de time pictures.
2 CONT
