1 OCCU Den moderna mineralogins grundläggare" och upptäckare av grundämnet nickel (NFamB).. Elev till Gottschalk Wallerius. Ledamot av Vetenskapsakademien 1765
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=15693
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Wikipedia Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT "...'''Baron Axel Fredrik Cronstedt''' ( December 23, 1722 – August 19, 1765) was a Swedish mineralogist and chemist who discovered nickel in 1751 as a mining expert with the Bureau of Mines. Cronstedt described it as kupfernickel
2 CONC . This name arises because the ore has a similar appearance to copper (kupfer) and a mischievous sprite (nickel) was supposed by miners to be the cause of their failure to extract copper from it. He was a pupil of Georg Brandt, th
2 CONC e discoverer of cobalt. Cronstedt is one of the founders of modern mineralogy[1] and is described as the founder by John Griffin in his 1827 A Practical Treatise on the Use of the Blowpipe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cronstedt also discovered the mineral scheelite in 1751. He named the mineral tungsten, meaning heavy stone in Swedish. Carl Wilhelm Scheele later suggested that a new metal could be extracted from the mineral. In English, this me
2 CONC tal is now known as the element tungsten.
2 CONT In 1753, Cronstedt was elected a member of the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences. In 1756, Cronstedt coined the term zeolite after heating the mineral stilbite with a blowpipe flame..."
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'': http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axel_Fredrik_Cronstedt
